                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6000b401-3bea-488e-8114-ce2e4bea9926",
                        "source_entry_id": "0c0b13b7-f69a-384d-b309-3e68f6610b85",
                        "target_lang_word": "slip away",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "slip away",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4fb37262-8afd-3c38-9b61-1681fcfdf52b",
                                        "entry_id": "bc7b7d38-b501-39f9-9eb1-d8bd07b872d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To leave without being noticed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d85aa9e-3bd5-41ae-b38b-709ee3f76e00",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb37262-8afd-3c38-9b61-1681fcfdf52b",
                                                "text": "I'm going to try to slip away from work early, if I can."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0082b74-250d-413a-b22e-6ea03710e302",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb37262-8afd-3c38-9b61-1681fcfdf52b",
                                                "text": "1906, Edith Nesbit, The Railway Children, Chapter 4: The engine-burglar,\nBut when Bobbie crept down later to bring up her presents--for she felt she really could not be separated from them all night--Mother was not writing, but leaning her head on her arms and her arms on the table. I think it was rather good of Bobbie to slip quietly away, saying over and over, \"She doesn't want me to know she's unhappy, and I won't know; I won't know.\" But it made a sad end to the birthday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48c40468-ac74-4b3e-8196-ea343c1e8a85",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb37262-8afd-3c38-9b61-1681fcfdf52b",
                                                "text": "When I'm tired and thinking cold\nI hide in my music, forget the day\nAnd dream of a girl I used to know\nI closed my eyes and she slipped away\nShe slipped away"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0c5525c-b95e-4763-9bee-c51a37b4f3e3",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb37262-8afd-3c38-9b61-1681fcfdf52b",
                                                "text": "He picked up his own phone, shunned limos and preferred to walk if possible (sciatica later caused him to use a wheelchair) – as, for example, on the day after his election when he slipped away on foot to collect his suitcase and settle the bill at the modest pensione where he had been booked in before the conclave began."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a8b5da9-1d40-375a-bddd-be69b576e96f",
                                        "entry_id": "bc7b7d38-b501-39f9-9eb1-d8bd07b872d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pass quickly, almost unnoticed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of time"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06f6b76a-0602-4098-a6c8-ad59dbe9e74d",
                                                "sense_id": "4a8b5da9-1d40-375a-bddd-be69b576e96f",
                                                "text": "The months slipped away and became years."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e8a81a9-3503-4eff-a18b-8e3677eff3f1",
                                                "sense_id": "4a8b5da9-1d40-375a-bddd-be69b576e96f",
                                                "text": "But with every word she was drawing further and further into herself, so he gave that up and only the dead dream fought on as the afternoon slipped away, trying to touch what was no longer tangible, struggling unhappily, undespairingly, toward that lost voice across the room."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "034bd6ae-81c6-35ec-96b1-c993c49c1bf2",
                                        "entry_id": "bc7b7d38-b501-39f9-9eb1-d8bd07b872d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disappear; to elude one; to recede; to dwindle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca80f3dc-6304-4d3e-be01-e424ed083be6",
                                                "sense_id": "034bd6ae-81c6-35ec-96b1-c993c49c1bf2",
                                                "text": "What about love?\nDon't you want someone to care about you?\nWhat about love?\nDon't let it slip away"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "350f8398-0b14-4fbb-8b58-8dac9fb26933",
                                                "sense_id": "034bd6ae-81c6-35ec-96b1-c993c49c1bf2",
                                                "text": "Scharner then headed a Dorrans free-kick against the crossbar, with Tchoyi unable to turn in the follow-up as the Baggies saw their hopes of salvaging a point slip away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "862aa6c9-51a1-47a7-9767-f6eb9269eda9",
                                                "sense_id": "034bd6ae-81c6-35ec-96b1-c993c49c1bf2",
                                                "text": "And there are few better ways to enjoy the rugged bleakness of the fells than from a nice warm train, especially when the weather's constantly changing as the day slips away."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb8b04d9-d1bf-3e31-8ea5-016b08611d32",
                                        "entry_id": "bc7b7d38-b501-39f9-9eb1-d8bd07b872d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To die peacefully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "euphemistic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "588a9c95-125c-4e63-91b2-33e24937b349",
                                                "sense_id": "eb8b04d9-d1bf-3e31-8ea5-016b08611d32",
                                                "text": "He slipped away quietly in his sleep."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
